Venetium 0074 - choose the browser icon (Venetium, its WinRT-style icon or your own .ico) and a real Start tile.

Asked for 2026-11-10: users wanted other icons, including other browsers' ones. The Chrome and Edge logos are their
owners' trademarks, so Venetium ships its own two icons and lets users bring any .ico of their own. 2 files:
- chrome/browser/win/app_icon.cc: when venetium-icon.ico lies beside venetium.exe and is a valid icon, GetAppIcon,
  GetSmallAppIcon and GetAppIconImageFamily load it instead of the built-in icon resource, so the browser windows, the
  taskbar button, the tray icon and the profile shortcut badges all show the chosen icon. The handles are new and owned
  by the caller (the callers already destroy them; the resource icon was shared, so destroying it was a no-op). The
  file is looked up once per run; without it nothing changes. The installer's icon page and set-icon.cmd write it, and
  point the Start / desktop shortcuts at it.
- chrome/app/visual_elements_resources/venetium.VisualElementsManifest.xml: the Start tile (Windows 8.1 and 10) in
  Venetium's navy, #182A4B, sampled from the icon's frame. Chromium only wrote this file from its own installer, so
  Venetium's zips shipped the tile pictures without it and Windows showed a plain default tile; the package now
  ships it beside venetium.exe. True live tiles need a Store app identity, which a desktop browser cannot have.

